<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cotton export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net Upland sales of 78,600 running bales (RB) slipped 19 percent below the previous week and 16 percent below the 4-week average.  The major increases were for China (34,000 RB), South Korea (15,400 RB), Taiwan (8,100 RB), Japan (7,500 RB), and Indonesia (6,900 RB).</p>
<p>Exports of 175,600 RB exceeded the previous week by 93 percent and the 4-week average by 27 percent.  Asian destinations accounted for 83 percent of the week's shipments; Western Hemisphere, 14 percent; and West European, 3 percent.</p>
</text>
